 "engine": "elevenlabs:scribe_v1",
 "text": "More money, same broke life. You were making $3,000 a month, and by the end of the month, every dollar was gone. Then boom, you get a raise. Now you're making five thousand. But what's the first thing you do? You get a nicer car, order more DoorDash, and start shopping whenever you feel like it. Before you know it, that extra $2,000 is gone too. Your paycheck went up, but your bank account didn't. That's called lifestyle inflation. Basically, every time you make more money, you find new ways to spend it. And look, there's nothing wrong with enjoying your money. But imagine saving just five hundred dollars of that raise every month. That's six thousand dollars in one year you could save, invest, or use to pay off debt. I'm learning that it's not just about making more money. It's about actually keeping some of it. Be real. Are you saving that raise or upgrading your lifestyle?",
